,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:848f916d50f54d540378f3eba684293fe7edf3a913015ab9f7da21c881b6ea69","file":"preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex","line":29,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7dc9abdf7cbc67fd670f2d4ef4eef85d4c2a77ca3a255c14915ff7205916eb8a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:848f916d50f54d540378f3eba684293fe7edf3a913015ab9f7da21c881b6ea69","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026/build/sections/00_intro.tex#L29"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet \\(A/\\Qbar\\) be an abelian variety of dimension \\(d\\) with good\nreduction \\(A_0/\\F\\) at \\(w\\). Let \\(0\\leq r\\leq d\\), and let\n\\[\n \\gamma\\in H^{2r}(A(\\C),\\Q(r))\n\\]\nbe a rational Hodge class. For every list of Cartier divisors\n\\(D_1,\\ldots,D_{d-r}\\) on \\(A_0\\), there is a number \\(q\\in\\Q\\)\nsuch that\n\\begin{align*}\n \\Tr_\\ell\\bigl(\\gamma_{0,\\ell}\n       c_{1,\\ell}(D_1)\\cdots c_{1,\\ell}(D_{d-r})\\bigr)&=q\n       &&\\text{in }\\Q_\\ell\\quad(\\ell\\ne p),\\\\\n \\Tr_p\\bigl(\\gamma_{0,p}\n       c_{1,\\mathrm{cris}}(D_1)\\cdots\n       c_{1,\\mathrm{cris}}(D_{d-r})\\bigr)&=q\n       &&\\text{in }\\Cw.\n\\end{align*}\nHere \\(\\gamma_{0,\\ell}\\) is the smooth proper specialization of the\n\\(\\ell\\)-adic realization, and \\(\\gamma_{0,p}\\) is the\nde Rham--crystalline specialization in\n\\[\n H^{2r}_{\\mathrm{cris}}(A_0/W(\\F))[1/p](r)\n       \\otimes_{\\Kzero}\\Cw.\n\\]\nThe traces use the top Tate twist and send the class of a zero-cycle to\nits degree. If \\(r=d\\), the divisor product is \\(1\\)."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:bca2c45b57481ad5b5d059dd8c87b56844ca413c83cb8d2d21a0e124c82ec3ef","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026#prop:transport","title":"Transport"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/ecae32f3877b3ab77718cc50.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Proposition","id":"r:Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026:prop:transport","manuscript_id":"p:Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026","name":"Transport","printed_number":"3.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","binding":{"file":"build/sections/02_transport.tex","label":"prop:transport","line":35,"manuscript":"Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026","statement_sha256":"f942c143ada5882512ed70536a5abef89c825634fb727d90e2d8de043b956534"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"f047bac96ee80ebef0b4f5a403831b84de6e32c1","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/Milnes-rationality-conjecture-for-abelian-varieties-October-7-2026.html#prop:transport","section":3,"section_title":"Transport through Hodge-type integral models","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:d158ff6d2f95a21880cc1449279c5cfdd0e538a4a8f9120df342f3bc2894f9d1","file":"preprin